FINDINGS:
1. True claims return SATISFIABLE (consistent), NOT VALID (entailed) — AR
   semantics; ar-check must treat SATISFIABLE as pass.
2. Translation is NON-DETERMINISTIC: R4 ran the byte-identical definition
   as R1 (hash d6704316ec34efb4…) and TC2 still flipped INVALID→AMBIGUOUS.
   Description prompt-shaping shifts which cases wobble; it does not
   eliminate variance.
3. SAFETY ENVELOPE (the property that holds in all 24 cells): valid tuples
   NEVER rejected (4/4 stable); invalid tuples NEVER pass — they land on
   INVALID or TRANSLATION_AMBIGUOUS only.
→ BINDING CONTRACT for Tasks 27/28 (ar-check.ts), embedded in the
   deliverable's _meta.arCheckGateMapping:
   pass = VALID|SATISFIABLE; reject+steered-retry = INVALID|IMPOSSIBLE;
   flag→HITL = TRANSLATION_AMBIGUOUS|NO_TRANSLATION|TOO_COMPLEX.
   Under this mapping every bad tuple ends in reject-or-HITL. ACC-3's
   mocked test (Task 35) should accept {INVALID → steered retry → HITL} as
   the primary path and treat AMBIGUOUS→HITL as an allowed live variant.

